WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.760
The saved Week 11 outline moves into a complex-scenario block. It does not introduce a new technical skill. The learner is expected to use previously taught assessment, airway, ventilation, vital-sign, communication and handover skills with less prompting.
学校保存的第11周纲要进入复杂情景模块，不增加新的技术技能。学员需要较少提示地运用之前学过的评估、气道、通气、生命体征、沟通及交接技能。

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:30.840
A classroom rehearsal can expose a gap and guide practice, but it does not certify competence. Perform physical skills only under instructor supervision and follow the school’s own checkoff standard.
课堂排练可以发现薄弱点并指导练习，但不能认证能力。身体技能只能在教师监督下练习，并遵循学校自己的考核标准。

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:44.832
The school asks for a thirty-minute PAA drill each day. A simple, repeatable frame helps the learner practise the decision sequence instead of spending the whole session resetting equipment or arguing about the script.
学校要求每天进行30分钟 PAA 练习。固定、可重复的流程能让学员练习决策顺序，而不是把整段时间都花在重置器材或争论台词上。

00:00:44.832 --> 00:01:02.664
At the start, identify which reference card or current pathway contains the newborn and child ventilation targets. Have one learner say the patient state and target aloud while another checks the reference; do not substitute normal breathing-rate ranges for assisted-ventilation rates.
开始时先确认哪张参考卡或现行流程列出新生儿及儿童通气目标。一名学员说出患者状态和目标，另一名核对原始参考；不要用正常呼吸频率替代辅助通气频率。

00:01:02.664 --> 00:01:19.560
Prepare the patient card, previously taught equipment and the relevant reference before starting the thirty-minute clock. The school specifies daily practice; the minute-by-minute division on the preceding slide is our suggested study arrangement, not a school marking rule.
开始30分钟计时前，准备患者卡、之前学过的器材及相关参考。学校要求每日练习；上一页的具体时间分配是本课程建议的学习安排，不是学校评分规则。

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:33.360
Give the observer two columns headed cue available and learner action. Record what actually happened, such as a breathing change followed by reassessment, rather than awarding credit because the learner later says they would have noticed it.
观察者分两栏记录“当时可用线索”和“学员行动”。记录实际发生的事，例如呼吸变化后进行了复评；不能因学员事后说自己本来会注意到，就算作已经做到。

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:46.392
After the first run, change one finding. Keep the rest of the history constant so the learner can explain why that specific change alters urgency, a partner task or the chosen pathway.
第一轮后只改变一项发现，其余病史保持一致，使学员能解释这一具体变化为何改变紧急程度、搭档任务或所选流程。

00:01:46.392 --> 00:01:59.256
Reserve the final minutes for one repeat of the affected decision. If the gap is a physical skill, take it to supervised practice; talking through a procedure is not evidence that the hands-on performance was safe.
最后几分钟重练受影响的一项决定。若缺口是身体操作，应安排受监督练习；口述操作不证明实际操作安全。

00:01:59.256 --> 00:02:15.552
Run the Priority Action Approach aloud. Begin with the scene and first impression, then assess the immediate threat, carry out the appropriate action and continue collecting useful information. If the patient deteriorates, return to the top of the decision loop.
大声运行优先行动法（PAA）：先评估现场及第一印象，再处理即时威胁、采取适当行动，并继续收集有用信息。患者恶化时，应返回决策循环起点重新判断。

00:02:15.552 --> 00:02:28.896
The observer should note whether the learner recognizes a threat without waiting for a mnemonic letter, delegates a clear task and checks the result. A correct acronym said at the wrong time is not effective patient care.
观察者应记录学员是否及时识别威胁而非等待口诀顺序、是否明确分工并确认结果。口诀背得正确但时机错误，并不等于有效照护。

00:02:28.896 --> 00:02:48.216
The drill must test the exact ventilation frequency for the patient state in the school’s assigned algorithm. Name whether the newborn is receiving initial positive-pressure ventilation or compressions, and whether the child is receiving rescue ventilation or CPR. These are not one generic “pediatric rate.”
练习应核查学校指定流程中、对应患者状态的准确通气频率。要说明新生儿是在接受初始正压通气还是胸外按压，也要说明儿童是在接受救援通气还是 CPR；不能统称为一个“儿科频率”。

00:02:48.216 --> 00:03:09.552
The saved school outline and the current BCEHS newborn algorithm use different initial ventilation ranges. The current linked algorithm lists 30 to 60 breaths per minute; the school outline records 40 to 60. Keep both labels visible, ask which version the class station tests, and never merge them into a third number.
学校保存的纲要与 BCEHS 当前新生儿算法，初始通气频率范围不同。当前链接算法列为每分钟30至60次；学校纲要列为40至60次。应明确标出两个版本，确认课堂站点考哪一版，不能把两者混成第三个数字。

00:03:09.552 --> 00:03:29.064
A ventilation number is not the only performance measure. Look for an appropriate seal, visible chest rise without excessive pressure, a controlled rhythm and a physiological response. Follow current BCEHS clinical direction in practice and the instructor’s stated exam revision for school assessment.
通气数字不是唯一表现指标。还要观察面罩密封、适当胸廓起伏且不过度加压、稳定节律及生理反应。临床实践遵循 BCEHS 现行指导；学校考核则按教师明确指定的考试版本。

00:03:29.064 --> 00:03:48.312
For a newborn requiring positive-pressure ventilation at birth, retrieve the initial ventilation branch rather than a normal resting respiratory range. The linked current BCEHS algorithm gives thirty to sixty per minute; the saved school outline gives forty to sixty. Keep the source labels attached.
出生时需要正压通气的新生儿，应查找初始通气分支，而不是正常静息呼吸范围。BCEHS 当前链接算法给出每分钟30至60次；保存的学校纲要给出40至60次。数值必须附有来源标签。

00:03:48.312 --> 00:04:07.344
When the birth-resuscitation algorithm calls for compressions, the coordinated three-to-one pattern is a different task. Do not continue counting initial ventilation breaths as though no compression branch had been entered. Revisit the Week Eight algorithm for entry criteria and effective-ventilation checks.
出生复苏算法要求按压时，协调3:1模式是另一项任务。不能进入按压分支后，仍像没有按压一样数初始通气次数。分支进入条件及有效通气检查见第8周算法。

00:04:07.344 --> 00:04:28.104
For an infant or child with a pulse and inadequate breathing who needs rescue breaths, the AHA and AAP twenty-twenty-five comparison gives twenty to thirty breaths a minute, approximately one every two to three seconds. It excludes newborn birth resuscitation and does not override a current indication to start CPR.
对有脉搏、呼吸不足且需要救援通气的婴儿或儿童，AHA/AAP 2025版对照给出每分钟20至30次，约每2至3秒一次。这不包括出生时新生儿复苏，也不覆盖当前需要开始CPR的适应症。

00:04:28.104 --> 00:04:51.024
Pediatric CPR without an advanced airway uses coordinated compression-breath cycles; with an advanced airway, the AHA comparison uses the twenty-to-thirty ventilation range. State the age, pulse and breathing condition, airway setup and source before giving a number. These are reference distinctions, not new permission to place an advanced airway.
未建立高级气道的儿科CPR使用协调按压通气周期；已建立高级气道时，AHA对照使用每分钟20至30次的通气范围。报数前说明年龄、脉搏与呼吸状态、气道装置及来源。这是参考情境区分，不是新增高级气道操作权限。

00:04:51.024 --> 00:05:07.416
Write two headings on the practice card: “school assessment” and “current service guideline.” Put each recalled target under its own heading and record the source. If the two values differ, pause and ask the instructor rather than silently correcting the card.
在练习卡上写两个标题：“学校考核”和“现行服务指南”。把记忆中的目标分开放入对应栏并记录来源。若数值不同，应停下来询问教师，而不是悄悄改掉练习卡。

00:05:07.416 --> 00:05:21.120
The newest web page is not proof that the school has changed its checkoff. The old school number is not proof that it is current clinical guidance. Separating the contexts is a clinical-safety and exam-accuracy skill.
网页更新较新，不代表学校已修改考核标准；学校旧数值也不代表它仍是临床现行指导。区分不同情境，是临床安全和考试准确性的一部分。

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:37.416
In this original rehearsal, a 58-year-old becomes confused after shopping. A witness reports that the patient has “sugar problems” but leaves before the crew can ask more. The patient reports abdominal discomfort and cannot name today’s medicines.
在这个原创排练中，一名58岁患者购物后出现意识混乱。目击者说患者有“血糖问题”，但救护人员尚未追问就离开。患者主诉腹部不适，也说不出今天服了哪些药。

00:05:37.416 --> 00:05:55.488
Do not stop the primary assessment while searching for a complete history. Address immediate threats, obtain vital signs and glucose when indicated, ask short focused questions and request collateral information from an available source. Record what is unknown as unknown.
不要因寻找完整病史而停止初步评估。应处理即时威胁、按需要测量生命体征和血糖、提出简短重点问题，并向可联系的信息来源获取旁证。未知内容应记录为未知。

00:05:55.488 --> 00:06:14.856
Return to the original grocery-parking-lot patient. Describe the findings without calling this a diabetic emergency: an adult with new confusion, weakness, discomfort and abnormal breathing, with an unconfirmed metabolic history. That statement remains accurate even if the witness was mistaken.
回到原创购物停车场患者。先描述发现，不直接称为糖尿病急症：成人出现新发意识混乱、虚弱、不适及异常呼吸，代谢病史尚未证实。即使目击者说错了，这一表述仍准确。

00:06:14.856 --> 00:06:33.000
Use a brief introduction and the primary assessment. Determine whether the patient can maintain the airway and adequate breathing, assess circulation and responsiveness, and obtain the indicated observations, including glucose. Do not allow the search for a medicine name to replace this assessment.
简短介绍后进行初步评估。判断患者能否维持气道及充分呼吸，评估循环和反应，并取得所需观察，包括血糖。寻找药名不能取代这些评估。

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:51.312
A clear partner request is: obtain the agreed observations and report any change in breathing or responsiveness immediately. A separate short question can establish the last known usual state. If nobody knows, record that limit rather than inventing an onset time.
可明确指派搭档：取得约定观察，并立即报告呼吸或反应变化。同时用简短问题询问最后正常状态。若无人知道，应记录局限，不得编造起病时间。

00:06:51.312 --> 00:07:06.552
State what must happen next even before the cause is known: address the current threat, choose the relevant authorized pathway, arrange appropriate help and movement, and continue focused history only when it does not delay necessary care.
即使病因未明，也应说明下一步：处理当前威胁、选择适当获准流程、安排所需支援及移动；仅在不延误必要照护时继续重点病史。

00:07:06.552 --> 00:07:24.960
A complex medical presentation can cross systems. Confusion may follow hypoxia, shock, metabolic change, medication effects, infection, injury or another cause. A single abnormal finding should sharpen the next question, not end the reasoning.
复杂内科表现可能涉及多个系统。意识混乱可能来自缺氧、休克、代谢改变、药物作用、感染、损伤或其他原因。单项异常应帮助提出下一个问题，而不是结束推理。

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:41.952
Build a short problem representation: what changed, when it changed, what is most abnormal now and what can deteriorate fastest. Use that summary to choose the current pathway and decide what history can safely be collected while transport is being prepared.
可用简短问题表述概括：发生了什么变化、何时变化、当前最异常的是什么、什么最可能迅速恶化。以此选择现行流程，并决定哪些病史可在准备转运时安全采集。

00:07:41.952 --> 00:07:59.472
In the first original update, the observer supplies a glucose result that does not explain the presentation and shows worsening breathing effort. The learner should move away from the witness-led assumption and assess the new breathing concern, not wait for a better diabetes history.
第一项原创变化中，观察者给出的血糖结果无法解释表现，同时患者呼吸努力加重。学员应摆脱目击者引导的假设、评估新的呼吸担忧，而不是等待更完整的糖尿病史。

00:07:59.472 --> 00:08:17.400
In a separate run, an appropriately measured low glucose is corrected through the relevant authorized pathway, but the patient remains confused. The treatment response is new evidence; it is not proof that every other cause has been excluded or that conveyance is unnecessary.
另一轮中，可靠测得的低血糖经适当获准流程纠正，但患者仍意识混乱。治疗反应是新证据，不证明其他原因均已排除，也不证明不需要转运。

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:33.792
Ask which findings improved, which did not and whether any new threat appeared. Reassess breathing, perfusion and responsiveness, and pursue the remaining problem through the actual pathway. Do not force the patient to fit the first explanation.
询问哪些发现改善、哪些未改善，以及是否出现新威胁。复评呼吸、灌注和反应，并按真实流程继续处理剩余问题。不能强迫患者符合最初解释。

00:08:33.792 --> 00:08:47.856
Give the receiving team an attributed timeline: the initial observations, the measured result, what was actually done and the repeated findings. Do not write resolved solely because one measurement moved toward normal.
向接收团队交代注明来源的时间线：初始观察、实测结果、实际行动及重复发现。不能因单个测量值趋向正常，就记录为问题已解决。

00:08:47.856 --> 00:09:05.016
The Sunday scenario intentionally creates competing demands. One learner leads while a partner supports two patients. The first task is not to assume the loudest patient is the sickest; make a rapid visual comparison and name immediate threats for both people.
周日情景刻意制造相互竞争的需求：一名学员负责带领，搭档协助两位患者。第一步不是假定声音最大的患者病情最重，而是快速比较两人并明确即时威胁。

00:09:05.016 --> 00:09:20.064
Assign one task at a time: “Check the second patient’s responsiveness and breathing, then report back.” Confirm the response. Keep visual contact and revisit the second patient when the first plan changes or new help arrives.
一次分派一项任务：“检查第二位患者的反应和呼吸，然后向我报告。”并确认执行结果。保持观察；第一位患者方案变化或新增支援到达时，要重新评估第二位患者。

00:09:20.064 --> 00:09:41.568
This is an original scene, not the school case. Two adults need help in a community-centre foyer. One is calling out about an ankle injury. The other is quiet, pale and visibly struggling to speak. Start by checking scene safety, access and the actual patient count, including whether there could be a common exposure.
这是原创情景，不是学校案例。社区中心门厅里两名成人需要帮助：一人因踝伤大声呼救，另一人安静、苍白且明显说话困难。首先检查安全、通道及真实患者数量，并考虑是否存在共同暴露。

00:09:41.568 --> 00:09:58.104
The quiet patient has a potentially immediate breathing threat and needs prompt assessment. Speaking in complete sentences is useful information about the injured patient at that moment, not a full clearance of their airway, circulation, injury or future course.
安静患者可能存在即时呼吸威胁，需要迅速评估。伤者此时能说完整句子是有用信息，但不代表其气道、循环、损伤及后续状态全部排除问题。

00:09:58.104 --> 00:10:16.080
Tell the partner to make a rapid primary check of Patient A and return a specific report, including any significant bleeding or change in responsiveness. The leader assesses Patient B. Request additional resources early with the number of patients and the current threat.
让搭档对患者A作快速初步检查，并具体报告，包括明显出血或反应变化；带领者评估患者B。应尽早请求额外资源，说明患者数量及当前威胁。

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:33.936
Do not pretend that two clinicians can perform four simultaneous procedures. Name who is providing the essential care, what can safely wait briefly and what requires another resource. Keep both patients within an active plan rather than letting the first allocation become permanent.
不能假装两名人员可同时完成四项操作。明确谁提供必要照护、什么可安全短暂等待、什么需要新增资源。两人都应纳入动态计划，不能把第一次分工作为永久安排。

00:10:33.936 --> 00:10:44.832
Say who is doing what and by when. A vague request such as “watch them” does not identify which observation matters or what should trigger a call for help.
明确说出谁负责什么以及何时完成。“看着他”这样的模糊要求没有说明要观察什么，也没有说明何时应请求支援。

00:10:44.832 --> 00:11:01.032
The partner repeats the task, completes it and reports the finding. The leader acknowledges the report and states the next action. If the partner cannot complete the task, that is important information; assign another safe action instead of assuming it happened.
搭档重复任务、完成操作并报告结果。带领者确认收到信息并说出下一步行动。若搭档无法完成任务，这本身就是重要信息；应改派另一项安全行动，而不是假设任务已经完成。

00:11:01.032 --> 00:11:18.360
A useful partner report might be: Patient A remains responsive, no major external bleeding found on the rapid check, and I have not yet completed the distal examination. This separates a limited check from a complete examination and makes unfinished work visible.
有用的搭档报告可表述为：患者A仍有反应，快速检查未发现大出血，远端检查尚未完成。这把有限检查与完整检查分开，也让未完成事项可见。

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:35.592
The leader acknowledges the report and assigns the next task in light of Patient B. If the partner cannot safely complete an action because essential breathing support requires two people, say that and update the resource and care plan; do not silently record the task as done.
带领者确认报告，并结合患者B情况安排下一任务。若必要呼吸支持需要两人，搭档无法安全完成另一行动，应明确说明并更新资源和照护计划，不能默认为已完成。

00:11:35.592 --> 00:11:53.664
A resource request should tell the responder what is needed, not just that the scene is busy. State two patients, the observed immediate threat, location and access, current staffing and the assistance required. An estimated arrival is not proof that the resource is present.
请求支援要说明需要什么，而不只是说现场很忙。应说明两位患者、观察到的即时威胁、位置及通道、现有人手和所需帮助。预计到达不代表已经到场。

00:11:53.664 --> 00:12:10.320
When help arrives, give each receiving clinician the patient-specific status and the next unresolved concern. Confirm acceptance of responsibility before changing roles, and avoid telling both new responders to help without naming which patient each owns.
支援到达后，向各接收人员交代对应患者状态及下一项未解决担忧。改变角色前确认对方接收责任；不能只让两名新人都去帮忙，却不指定各自负责谁。

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:27.480
A scenario may change when a second patient collapses, the exit becomes blocked or additional resources arrive. Pause for a short scene scan, state the new risk and update the team. Continuing the original plan without checking the change is not autonomy.
当第二位患者倒下、出口受阻或新增支援到达时，情景可能发生变化。应短暂停下来扫描现场，说出新风险并更新团队。没有确认变化就继续原计划，不算自主判断。

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:43.512
Protect your partner and both patients. If the environment becomes unsafe or the team lacks the training or equipment needed, withdraw to a safe position and request help. Do not turn a simulation target into permission to take an uncontrolled risk.
保护搭档及两位患者。若现场变得不安全，或团队缺少必要培训、器材，应退至安全位置并请求支援。不能把模拟训练目标变成承担失控风险的许可。

00:12:43.512 --> 00:13:00.792
Reveal the first change only after the learner has stated the initial plan: Patient B becomes less responsive. Stop nonessential interviewing and reassess immediate threats. A quieter patient after a struggle may be deteriorating rather than settling.
学员说明初始计划后才揭示第一项变化：患者B反应下降。停止非必要访谈并复评即时威胁。费力呼吸后变得更安静，可能是恶化而非平稳。

00:13:00.792 --> 00:13:16.152
Tell the partner what changed, which task now has priority and who is maintaining observation of Patient A. If the existing team cannot meet both needs, communicate the resource gap explicitly and request the appropriate urgent support.
告诉搭档发生了什么、哪项任务现在优先，以及谁继续观察患者A。若现有人手无法满足双方需求，应明确沟通资源缺口并请求适当紧急支援。

00:13:16.152 --> 00:13:35.616
For a different repeat, keep Patient B unchanged and reveal new numbness in Patient A’s injured foot. A limb problem that was initially less urgent now needs a repeat distal assessment and a revised plan. Do not assume a splint or position remains safe merely because it was acceptable earlier.
另一轮保持患者B不变，揭示患者A伤足新发麻木。最初紧急程度较低的肢体问题，现在需要重复远端评估并修订计划。不能因夹板或体位先前可接受，就假定现在仍安全。

00:13:35.616 --> 00:13:52.368
Report the finding before and after the relevant action, with the time and any part that cannot be assessed. Reprioritize from the current evidence for both patients; this is not an automatic instruction to abandon one patient or perform an untrained reduction.
报告相关行动前后的发现、时间及无法评估的部分。依据双方当前证据重排优先级；这不意味着自动弃置其中一人，也不授权进行未经培训的复位。

00:13:52.368 --> 00:14:08.232
The school asks for a shared debrief. Each learner should first describe their own observation and reasoning before hearing the group’s interpretation. This makes missed cues, assumptions and good decisions visible without turning the conversation into blame.
学校要求共同复盘。每位学员先描述自己的观察和推理，再听取小组的解释。这样可以看见遗漏线索、假设及正确决策，而不把讨论变成指责。

00:14:08.232 --> 00:14:24.120
Ask “What did you know at that moment?” rather than judging from facts revealed later. Name one action to preserve and one specific change for the next run. If a skill gap appears, record it for instructor-led practice and checkoff.
应问“当时你掌握了什么信息？”，而不是用后来才揭示的事实评判当时决策。指出一项值得保持的行动和下次要改进的具体点。发现技能缺口时，应记录并安排教师指导练习及考核。

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:42.024
Begin with each person’s account. For this original scene, the learner may say: I focused on the ankle because that patient spoke first, and I did not notice the quiet patient’s incomplete speech until the partner pointed it out. That identifies a specific attention error, not a character flaw.
先听每人叙述。本原创场景中，学员可说：伤者先开口，所以我集中在踝部；直到搭档指出，我才注意到安静患者说话不完整。这指出具体注意分配错误，而非人格缺陷。

00:14:42.024 --> 00:14:59.496
Ask what information was available before that decision. The corrective plan is to compare immediate threats in both patients, name the first priority and assign the other rapid check with an expected report. Do not repair the problem merely by making the next script longer.
询问作决定前有哪些可用信息。改进计划是比较两人的即时威胁、明确首要优先项，并安排另一人的快速检查和预期报告。不能只靠把下一份台词写长来修复问题。

00:14:59.496 --> 00:15:14.568
On the repeat, the observer records whether the comparison occurred before detailed interviewing and whether the partner’s result was actually used. This tests the proposed repair without inventing a pass score or assuming confidence equals competence.
重练时，观察者记录详细访谈前是否作了比较、是否真实使用搭档结果。这检验所提改进，不发明及格分，也不把自信当作能力。

00:15:14.568 --> 00:15:32.952
Close by naming one preserved strength and one remaining gap, with a practical next action. Carry a technical gap to the instructor; carry an unclear source version to the reference card. A debrief ends with a changed action, not only an agreement that the case was difficult.
结束时指出一项保留优点、一项剩余缺口及具体下一行动。技术缺口交给教师处理，来源版本不清则回到参考卡核查。复盘应产生行动改变，而不仅是大家同意案例很难。

00:15:32.952 --> 00:15:48.960
The observer should write an exact phrase or action that shows the skill. “Looked confident” is too vague to coach. Better evidence is “noticed falling responsiveness, stopped the history questions and asked the partner to prepare urgent movement.”
观察者应记录能体现技能的具体话语或行动。“看起来有自信”过于模糊，无法用于指导。更好的证据是：“发现反应下降后停止追问病史，并让搭档准备紧急搬动。”

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:59.952
Use the school rubric if one is supplied. This card is a rehearsal prompt, not an invented grading standard, and it does not replace the instructor’s formal assessment.
若学校提供评分表，应使用学校评分表。本卡只是排练提示，不是另设评分标准，也不能代替教师正式考核。

00:15:59.952 --> 00:16:16.584
The Week 11 block develops autonomy through repeated use of skills already taught. Practise the PAA, retrieve the correct newborn or pediatric ventilation target, prioritize the most urgent change, coordinate with a partner and debrief from evidence.
第11周模块通过反复使用既有技能培养自主判断。练习 PAA，查找正确的新生儿或儿科通气目标，优先处理最紧急变化，与搭档协调，并依据事实复盘。

00:16:16.584 --> 00:16:29.376
Next, the reading workshop links every school-assigned Week 11 reading row to a bilingual study guide. Candidate-edition differences and current clinical guidance will remain clearly separated.
下一课的阅读工作坊会把学校指定的全部第11周阅读条目连接到双语学习指南，并明确区分候选教材版本差异与当前临床指导。
